  agent spawned at pave-init:adversarial-investigator with no name. It gets
  plugin_root, the primary artifacts, and one decision question, and returns
  a verdict with file:line evidence. The roles lists of 9 nodes, the
  escalation principle, and the fallback ladder question follow. (2)
  fallback_ladder_exhausted points to its owner, references/validation-defaults.md
  section Per-BS Verdicts and Track-Level Fallback Ladder, in place of
  references/impl-track-rules.md, and defines the RETRY_WITH_CONTINGENCY
  rung (R12): one named fallback, implemented once, reruns Gates 5.1a to 5.2.
  (3) pre_ship_checks_passed lists the four checks of
  orchestration/integration-logic.md: no conflict markers in the added
  integration diff lines, no REGRESSED or CATASTROPHIC in
  integration.per_bs_verdict, opt.returncode == 0 on every integration sweep
  row, and ammo_state.py validate passes. Same strength as before, named
  exactly. (4) stage_1_baseline: the lead runs scripts/ammo_state.py
  ingest-baseline on the baseline sweep before T_AUDIT_S1, so the auditor
  reads the ingested numbers. (5) audit_s45: the early per-track partial
  step goes (R9, user ruling that amends decision 4; nothing read the
  partials). (6) stage_7b_report re-entry: a terminal campaign re-enters
  Stage 7b when REPORT.md is absent or has no accepted
  report_fact_check.json (ok true, report_sha256 of the current REPORT.md).
  The old text re-entered only when REPORT.md was absent. The Claude and
  Codex stop guards and the next-step reminder check the same condition.
  (7) Fact-check wording: role report_fact_checker, evidence
  report_fact_check, and check report_fact_check_ok call the fact-checker's
  list findings, not violations, matching the returned findings field in
  agents/ammo-report-writer.md. (8) audit_s67_passed: the passing verdict
  is the file that audit.stage_67.verdict_file names (stage_67.md for the
  first cycle, stage_67_cycle_{C}.md for a re-audit), in place of a copy to
  the canonical stage_67.md; the copy step went (w6-8,
  orchestration/audit-protocol.md).
